WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.824
Failure Handling. Failure handling defines what an AI system should do when the expected result is not produced.

00:00:07.824 --> 00:00:19.800
Definition. Possible responses include retrying, using a fallback, asking for missing information, returning an error, requesting human review, or stopping safely.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:29.376
Think of it like. A building defines what people do when power fails or a route is blocked; AI systems need clear paths for failure too.

00:00:29.376 --> 00:00:40.560
How it works. Check errors, timeouts, schema, and evidence; separate transient, input, tool, and safety failures; then log the event.

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:50.592
Example. Retry or return a validation error for invalid JSON; use a fallback or ask the user to try later after a tool timeout.

00:00:50.592 --> 00:00:58.632
Remember. Retry is only one response; safe handling also includes fallback, review, and stop.
